Final CSS project: a polished **profile card** that puts selectors, flexbox, grid, and transforms together.

### The card layout
```css
.card {
  max-width: 320px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  border-radius: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}
```
`overflow: hidden` keeps the avatar's rounded corners clean.

### Centering with flexbox
```css
.card-body {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 24px;
}
```

### Circular avatar
```css
.avatar {
  width: 96px;
  height: 96px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  object-fit: cover;   /* crop instead of stretch */
}
```

### Hover lift
```css
.card {
  transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
}
.card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-6px);
  box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
}
```
The card gently floats up on hover — a classic premium-feel interaction.

### Badges with flexbox + gap
```css
.skills {
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
}
.skill {
  background: #f3f4f6;
  border-radius: 9999px;
  padding: 4px 12px;
  font-size: 12px;
}
```

Combine these patterns and you have a component that looks like a real product UI.
